/-!
# Cusp-label embedding of the base-changed modular function field

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.exists_algHom_laurentBaseChange_slot`
(`a2de6957-8b55-5abe-9d8d-ab2b90d24e87`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `7fced64d-979b-58ce-a91c-dc2288b3bb24`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero (a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra), let $N \geq 1$, and let $\zeta
\in K^{\times}$ be a unit whose underlying element of $K$ is a primitive $N$-th root of unity. Let
$a, b$ be natural numbers with $a \mid N$, $a \neq 0$, $b < N/a$, and $\gcd(\gcd(a,b), N/a) = 1$.
Write $j(q) = q^{-1}\sum_{n \geq 0} c_n q^n$ for the Laurent series `jq` over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the
single term $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`), let `qExpand R M` be the substitution $f(q)
\mapsto f(q^{M})$ on Laurent series, `qTwist u` the substitution $f(q) \mapsto f(uq)$, and `coeffEmb
K` the coefficientwise map $K((q)) \leftarrow \mathbb{Q}((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to K$. Then
there is a $K$-algebra homomorphism $\iota$ from the intermediate field `laurentBaseChange K
(modularFunctionFieldFull N)` of $K((q))$ — the field generated over $K$ by the image under
`coeffEmb K` of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the series $j(q^{d})$
for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$ — into $K((q))$, such that $\iota$ sends the element $j(q)$ to
$j(q^{N})$ and sends the element $j(q^{N})$ to $j(\zeta^{ab} q^{a^{2}})$, i.e. to `qExpand K (a * a)
(qTwist (ζ ^ (b * a)) (coeffEmb K jq))`. Only these two values are asserted; no uniqueness claim is
made.

Classically this is the expansion, at the cusp labelled by the primitive pair $(a,b)$ with $a \mid
N$, of the function field of $X_0(N)$ over $K$, realised as an embedding into a Laurent series field
in the parameter playing the role of $q^{1/N}$; the second generator becomes the expansion of
$j((a\tau + b)/(N/a))$. It is used in the counting of cusps and in the analysis of fibres of the
Hecke correspondence on $X_0(N)$.

